$privacyWithComments = <<<'HTML'
<p>Effective Date: July 27, 2026. Website: https://bbafoundation.com/</p>
<p>At BBA Foundation, we are committed to protecting the privacy and personal data of our visitors, partners, and scholarship applicants. This Privacy Policy outlines how we collect, use, store, and protect your personal information when you visit our website or apply for our scholarship programs.</p>
<h2>Who We Are</h2>
<p>Our website address is: https://bbafoundation.com/. BBA Foundation provides educational opportunities and financial support to eligible students across Ekiti State.</p>
<h2>What Personal Data We Collect and Why</h2>
<h3>1. Scholarship Application Uploads</h3>
<p>When applying for our scholarship, students are required to download the application form, complete it, and upload a single compressed folder (ZIP archive) containing all supporting documentation. The personal data collected within this uploaded package includes: Completed Application Form: Personal details such as full name, date of birth, gender, home address, local government area (LGA) of origin in Ekiti State, phone number, and email address. Academic Records: School name, course of study, student identification details, academic transcripts, and official examination results. Supporting Identification: Digital copies of official means of identification (e.g., Student ID card, Voter's Card, National Identity Number slip, or State ID). Passport Photograph: Digital passport image for identity verification. Reference &amp; Recommendation Letters: Scanned letters and contact details of referees, academic heads, or community leaders providing references on your behalf. Why we collect this: This information is collected strictly to verify applicant eligibility, assess financial need, conduct candidate screening, award scholarships, and communicate selection outcomes.</p>
<h3>2. Comments</h3>
<p>When visitors leave comments on the site, we collect the data shown in the comments form, as well as the visitor's IP address and browser user agent string to assist in spam detection. An anonymized string created from your email address (also called a hash) may be provided to the Gravatar service to see if you are using it. The Gravatar service privacy policy is available here: https://automattic.com/privacy/. After approval of your comment, your profile picture is visible to the public in the context of your comment.</p>
<h3>3. Media &amp; File Upload Security</h3>
<p>When preparing your ZIP folder for upload: Embedded Location Data: Avoid uploading image files (such as passport photos or ID scans) that contain embedded GPS location data (EXIF GPS). Archive Security: Uploaded ZIP folders are routed directly to secure server directories and are accessed exclusively by authorized review personnel.</p>
<h3>4. Contact Forms</h3>
<p>When you reach out to us via our online contact forms, we collect your name, email address, and message contents solely to respond to your inquiry.</p>
<h3>5. Cookies</h3>
<p>Comments cookies (1 year, if enabled); Login Information: If you visit our login page, we set a temporary cookie to determine if your browser accepts cookies. This cookie contains no personal data and is discarded when you close your browser. When you log in, several cookies are set up to save your login information and screen display choices. Login cookies last for two days, and screen options cookies last for a year. If you select "Remember Me", your login will persist for two weeks. Logging out removes these cookies. Content Editing cookie (1 day).</p>
<h3>6. Embedded Content from Other Websites</h3>
<p>Articles on this site may include embedded content (e.g., videos, images, maps, or embedded PDF viewers). Embedded content from other websites behaves in the exact same way as if the visitor visited the other website directly. These websites may collect data about you, use cookies, embed additional third-party tracking, and monitor your interaction with that content, particularly if you have an account and are logged in to that website.</p>
<h2>Who We Share Your Data With</h2>
<p>We prioritize applicant confidentiality. Your personal information, passport photographs, ID documents, ZIP archives, and recommendation letters are never sold, rented, or traded to third parties. Scholarship Selection Committee: Uploaded ZIP archives are extracted and reviewed internally by authorized members of the BBA Foundation review committee and board for screening and verification. Educational Institutions &amp; Verification Bodies: We may contact schools, institutions, or referees listed in your application solely to verify your academic standing and eligibility. Administrative Security: If you request a password reset on our platform, your IP address will be included in the reset email. Spam Detection: Visitor comments may be checked through an automated spam detection service.</p>
<h2>How Long We Retain Your Data</h2>
<p>Scholarship Records &amp; Uploads: ZIP files and extracted application documents submitted by candidates are retained for as long as necessary to administer the scholarship award, fulfill auditing requirements, or maintain alumni records for successful scholars. Data of non-selected applicants is securely deleted or archived after the annual selection cycle concludes. Comments: If you leave a comment, the comment and its metadata are retained indefinitely to recognize and approve follow-up comments automatically. User Profiles: For users who register on our website (if any), we store the personal information provided in their user profile. All users can see, edit, or delete their personal information at any time (except they cannot change their username). Website administrators can also view and edit that information.</p>
<h2>What Rights You Have Over Your Data</h2>
<p>If you have submitted a scholarship application, uploaded a ZIP archive, have an account on this site, or have left comments, you have the right to: Request an exported file of the personal data we hold about you, including any data you have provided to us. Request that we correct, update, or erase any personal data or uploaded application files we hold about you. Note: This does not include any data we are obliged to keep for administrative, legal, auditing, or security purposes.</p>
<h2>How We Protect Your Data</h2>
<p>We implement strong physical, technical, and administrative security measures to safeguard your uploaded files and sensitive personal data. Uploaded ZIP files are stored in protected directories on our servers with restricted access permissions. Only designated selection committee members have access to download and uncompress applicant files. We use encrypted website connections (HTTPS/SSL) to protect all uploads in transit.</p>
<h2>Data Breach Procedures</h2>
<p>In the event of an identified security breach affecting your personal data or uploaded application files, BBA Foundation will promptly take steps to contain the breach, notify affected applicants via email, and report the incident to relevant regulatory authorities as required by applicable data protection laws.</p>
<h2>Contact Information</h2>
<p>For any questions, requests regarding your data, or inquiries regarding the scholarship application process, please contact us at: Website: https://bbafoundation.com/ Email: info@bbafoundation.com</p>
HTML;

